@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `usca-operation-of-statutes`

-- California defined terms: the definitions of the Government Code, the Civil Code and the Code of Civil Procedure, as a table of
-- (code, term, how it is defined, what it names, what it excludes), and the definitions that need facts instead of a list of members.
--
-- Added in pass 2 of the completion to "whole".  Pass 1 left the one-line definitions inert; the brief says a definition is encoded: a function
-- that returns the term's meaning as the text states it (the members it names, what it includes or excludes, what it points at), with a test for each entry.
-- Sources: Gov. Code §§ 12.2, 15, 17, 19, 20, 21, 22, 26; Civ. Code § 14(a), (b); Code Civ. Proc. §§ 14, 17(b).
-- The quotation lines are copied by script from the converter-made plain-text rendering of the sections (not the official text) and checked
-- against it by srcrefs.py.  Target: unstable (REFUSE).  Imports: prelude and usca-operation-of-statutes (for `Kind of code`).
--
-- Two ways of defining.  A definition by inclusion (`includes`, `signifies` is read the same way only where noted) names some members and does not
-- say there are no others: a thing outside the list is REFUSED, not FALSE.  A definition by meaning (`means`, `is coextensive with`) is closed:
-- a thing outside the list is FALSE.  A thing a definition expressly excludes (Gov. Code § 20) is FALSE under either.
-- The three codes use the same words for different lists (not a fork: each list is encoded as its code states it; Gov. Code § 17 names eight kinds of person, Civ. Code § 14(a) and Code Civ. Proc.
-- § 17(b)(6) name the corporation), so every lookup takes the code.

§ `The table of defined terms`

DECLARE `Kind of definition` IS ONE OF
    `a definition by inclusion`
    `a definition by meaning`

DECLARE `Definition of a term` HAS
    `the code`           IS A `Kind of code`
    `the term`           IS A STRING
    `how it is defined`  IS A `Kind of definition`
    `what it names`      IS A LIST OF STRING
    `what it excludes`   IS A LIST OF STRING

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:51 | 12.2. “Spouse” includes “registered domestic partner,” as required by Section 297.5 of the Family Code.
@ref Gov. Code § 12.2 (src:GOV-ss-1-26:51)
GIVETH A `Definition of a term`
`Gov. Code § 12.2: spouse` MEANS
    `Definition of a term` WITH
        `the code` IS `the Government Code`
        `the term` IS "spouse"
        `how it is defined` IS `a definition by inclusion`
        `what it names` IS (LIST "registered domestic partner")
        `what it excludes` IS (EMPTY)

