       , `Civ. Code § 14(b)(7): spouse`
       , `Code Civ. Proc. § 14: seal`
       , `Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(2): county`
       , `Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(5): oath`
       , `Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(6): person`
       , `Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(8): property`
       , `Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(8)(A): personal property`
       , `Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(8)(B): real property`
       , `Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(10): sheriff`
       , `Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(12): spouse`
       , `Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(14): will`
       , `Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(16): writing`

-- The entry of the table for a term in a code, if the deposit defines it there.
GIVEN code IS A `Kind of code`
      term IS A STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF `Definition of a term`
`the entries of the table for the term in` code `being` term MEANS
    filter (GIVEN d YIELD d's `the code` EQUALS code AND d's `the term` EQUALS term) `the table of defined terms`

GIVEN term IS A STRING
      code IS A `Kind of code`
      thing IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the term in the code names` term `in` code `the thing` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER `the entries of the table for the term in` code `being` term
    WHEN EMPTY THEN REFUSE "no deposited section of that code defines that term"
    WHEN d FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        BRANCH
            IF elem thing (d's `what it names`) THEN TRUE
            IF elem thing (d's `what it excludes`) THEN FALSE
            IF d's `how it is defined` EQUALS `a definition by meaning` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE REFUSE "the section defines the term by inclusion, naming some members; it does not say whether this thing is another"

§ `Process: Gov. Code § 22, Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(7)`

DECLARE `Kind of document` IS ONE OF
    writ
    summons
    `some other document`

DECLARE `Nature of a judicial proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `a proceeding of a civil nature`
    `a proceeding of a criminal nature`
    `a proceeding of some other nature`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:86 | 22. “Process” includes a writ or summons issued in the course of judicial proceedings of either a civil or criminal nature.
-- Gov. Code § 22 says process "includes" a writ or summons issued in the course of judicial proceedings of either a civil or criminal nature: a
-- definition by inclusion, so anything else is REFUSED.  Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(7) says it "signifies" a writ or summons issued in the course of
-- a judicial proceeding, with no word about the nature of the proceeding: read as a closed definition, so anything else is FALSE (fork F-process).
@ref Gov. Code § 22 (src:GOV-ss-1-26:86)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of document`
      `it is issued in the course of judicial proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      nature IS A `Nature of a judicial proceeding`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a document is process under Gov. Code § 22` kind `issued in the course of judicial proceedings:` `it is issued in the course of judicial proceedings` `of the nature` nature MEANS
    IF     (kind EQUALS writ OR kind EQUALS summons)
       AND `it is issued in the course of judicial proceedings`
       AND (nature EQUALS `a proceeding of a civil nature` OR nature EQUALS `a proceeding of a criminal nature`)
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Gov. Code § 22 says process includes a writ or summons issued in the course of judicial proceedings of a civil or criminal nature; it does not say what else is or is not process"

-- src:CCP-ss-1-34:70 | (7) “Process” signifies a writ or summons issued in the course of a judicial proceeding.
@ref Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(7) (src:CCP-ss-1-34:70)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of document`
      `it is issued in the course of a judicial proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a document is process under Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(7)` kind `issued in the course of a judicial proceeding:` `it is issued in the course of a judicial proceeding` MEANS
    (kind EQUALS writ OR kind EQUALS summons) AND `it is issued in the course of a judicial proceeding`

§ `Testify and depose: Civ. Code § 14(a), Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(5)`

DECLARE `Form of a statement` IS ONE OF
    oral
    written

DECLARE `Term for a statement under oath` IS ONE OF
    testify
    depose

-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:57 | 14. (a) Words used in this code in the present tense include the future as well as the present; words used in the masculine gender include the feminine and neuter; the singular number includes the plural, and the plural the singular; the word person includes a corporation as well as a natural person; county includes city and county; writing includes printing and typewriting; oath includes affirmation or
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:58 | declaration; and every mode of oral statement, under oath or affirmation, is embraced by the term “testify,” and every written one in the term “depose”; signature or subscription includes mark, when the person cannot write, his name being written near it, by a person who writes his own name as a witness; provided, that when a signature is by mark it must in order that the same may be acknowledged or may serve as the signature to any sworn statement be witnessed by two persons who must subscribe their own names as witnesses thereto.
-- src:CCP-ss-1-34:66 | (A) “Depose” includes any written statement made
-- src:CCP-ss-1-34:67 | under oath or affirmation.
-- src:CCP-ss-1-34:68 | (B) “Testify” includes any mode of oral statement made under oath or affirmation.
-- Civ. Code § 14(a): "every mode of oral statement, under oath or affirmation, is embraced by the term 'testify,' and every written one in the term 'depose'".
-- Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(5)(A), (B): "Depose" includes any written statement made under oath or affirmation; "Testify" includes any mode of oral statement
-- made under oath or affirmation.  Both define by inclusion, so a statement outside the two pairings is REFUSED; the Government Code has no such section.
@ref Civ. Code § 14(a), Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(5)(A), (B) (src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:57-58, src:CCP-ss-1-34:66-68)
GIVEN code IS A `Kind of code`
      term IS A `Term for a statement under oath`
      form IS A `Form of a statement`
      `it is made under oath or affirmation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the term embraces the statement, in` code term `being` form `made under oath or affirmation:` `it is made under oath or affirmation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF code EQUALS `the Government Code`
            THEN REFUSE "the Government Code has no deposited section that defines testify or depose"
        IF `it is made under oath or affirmation` AND term EQUALS testify AND form EQUALS oral THEN TRUE
        IF `it is made under oath or affirmation` AND term EQUALS depose AND form EQUALS written THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE REFUSE "Civ. Code § 14(a) and Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(5) say testify includes any oral statement under oath or affirmation and depose any written one; they do not say what else either term includes"

§ `Writ: Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(15)`

DECLARE `In whose name an order is issued` IS ONE OF
    `the name of the people`
    `the name of a court`
    `the name of a judicial officer`
    `the name of someone else`

-- src:CCP-ss-1-34:81 | (15) “Writ” means an order or precept in writing, issued in the name of the people, or of a court or judicial officer.
@ref Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(15) (src:CCP-ss-1-34:81)
GIVEN `it is an order or precept` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      name IS AN `In whose name an order is issued`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a document is a writ` `it is an order or precept` `it is in writing` `it is issued in` name MEANS
    `it is an order or precept` AND `it is in writing` AND NOT (name EQUALS `the name of someone else`)

§ `Affinity: Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(1)`

-- src:CCP-ss-1-34:61 | (1) “Affinity” signifies the connection existing in consequence of marriage, between each of the married persons and the blood relatives of the other when applied to the marriage relation.
@ref Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(1) (src:CCP-ss-1-34:61)
GIVEN `it is a connection existing in consequence of marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is between a married person and the blood relatives of the other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the word is applied to the marriage relation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a connection is affinity` `it is a connection existing in consequence of marriage` `it is between a married person and the blood relatives of the other` `the word is applied to the marriage relation` MEANS
    `it is a connection existing in consequence of marriage` AND `it is between a married person and the blood relatives of the other` AND `the word is applied to the marriage relation`

§ `Recycled water: Gov. Code § 26`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:96 | 26. For the purposes of this code, “recycled water” or “reclaimed water” has the same meaning as recycled water as defined in subdivision (n) of Section 13050 of the Water Code.
-- The meaning is in Water Code § 13050(n), which is not deposited: it is asked as an input and returned for both terms.
@ref Gov. Code § 26 (src:GOV-ss-1-26:96)
GIVEN term IS A STRING
      `the meaning of recycled water given by subdivision (n) of Section 13050 of the Water Code` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the meaning in the Government Code of` term `given that Water Code § 13050(n) defines recycled water as:` `the meaning of recycled water given by subdivision (n) of Section 13050 of the Water Code` MEANS
    IF term EQUALS "recycled water" OR term EQUALS "reclaimed water"
    THEN `the meaning of recycled water given by subdivision (n) of Section 13050 of the Water Code`
    ELSE REFUSE "Gov. Code § 26 defines recycled water and reclaimed water only"

§ `United States: Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(13)`

DECLARE `Part of the United States` IS ONE OF
    `the District of Columbia`
    `the territories`
    `a state`

-- src:CCP-ss-1-34:79 | (13) “State” includes the District of Columbia and the territories when applied to the different parts of the United States, and the words “United States” may include the district and territories.
-- The first half of the entry, "State" includes the District of Columbia and the territories when applied to the different parts of the United States,
-- is `the meaning of State in the Government Code` in usca-general-provisions.l4 (Gov. Code § 18 says the same).  The second half is here.
@ref Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(13) (src:CCP-ss-1-34:79)
GIVEN part IS A `Part of the United States`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the words United States may include` part MEANS
    CONSIDER part
    WHEN `the District of Columbia` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the territories` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a state` THEN REFUSE "Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(13) says the words United States may include the district and territories; it does not say what else they may or may not include"
